  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef dl_gan_training(real_data: list, noise: list, W_gen: list, W_disc: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **GAN Training Step** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef dl_gan_training(real_data: list, noise: list, W_gen: list, W_disc: list) -> dict:\n    Xr, z, Wg, Wd = np.array(real_data, dtype=np.float64), np.array(noise, dtype=np.float64), np.array(W_gen, dtype=np.float64), np.array(W_disc, dtype=np.float64)\n    sigm = lambda v: 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-np.clip(v, -20.0, 20.0)))\n    dr, df = sigm(np.dot(Xr, Wd)), sigm(np.dot(np.dot(z, Wg), Wd))\n    return {'d_loss': round(float(-np.mean(np.log(np.clip(dr, 1e-12, 1.0)) + np.log(np.clip(1.0 - df, 1e-12, 1.0)))), 4), 'g_loss': round(float(-np.mean(np.log(np.clip(df, 1e-12, 1.0)))), 4), 'd_real_mean': round(float(np.mean(dr)), 4), 'd_fake_mean': round(float(np.mean(df)), 4)}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
